## What questions should I ask my SEO agency before renewing?

The review gives you a list of questions tailored to your site and your reports. These are the seven I find most useful in general:

1. Which pages did you change in the last six months, and what changed on each one?
2. Which of those changes can you link to a rise in clicks or enquiries in Search Console or GA4?
3. Which sites did the links you built come from, and how were they obtained?
4. What were the three biggest problems on our site when you started, and which are now fixed?
5. How do you count leads in your reports, and does that match what our sales team sees?
6. What would you do differently next year, and what will it cost?
7. If we leave, do we keep the content, the accounts and the data?

The answers matter more than the questions. The two panels show what a good answer and a red-flag answer look like.

{% panels %}
{% panel eyebrow="Good answer" title="Specific, dated and checkable" tone="good" %}
- Names the pages changed and the month each change went live
- Shows the change on the live site
- Links each change to Search Console clicks or enquiries before and after
- Lists the sites that links came from and how they were obtained
{% /panel %}
{% panel eyebrow="Red flag answer" title="Vague or built on numbers you cannot check" tone="bad" %}
- Talks about ongoing optimisation without naming a page
- Leads with Domain Authority or keyword counts padded with your own brand name
- Reports links as a number with no list of sites
- Repeats the same open issues month after month
{% /panel %}
{% /panels %}

A good agency will answer these quickly and with evidence. Vague answers are useful information too.

## What does the review not include?

My independent SEO agency review does not include managing your agency, attending meetings with them or negotiating the contract. I also do not review PPC or paid social work. The review covers SEO and AI search only.

Implementation is not included. The findings are yours to share with your agency, your developer or your team.

## What happens after the review?

The 60-minute walkthrough at the end of my SEO agency review finishes with a recommended next step. The usual outcomes are:

- **Renew with a sharper scope:** keep the agency and use the findings to agree clearer deliverables and reporting
- **Renegotiate:** keep the agency on a smaller or different scope where some of the work is not paying back
- **Move in-house with support:** your team does the work with direction from me through SEO consulting at £200 per session or £600 per month
- **Switch provider:** brief a new agency or consultant using the findings as the starting baseline

My [SEO retainer](/services/seo-retainer/) starts at £1,500 per month if you want me to take on the work. The £495 is credited against your first month if you start a retainer within 60 days of delivery. There is no obligation to do so.

