## Frequently asked questions

### Will my agency know you are reviewing their work?

Your agency will only know about my review if you tell them. I use read-only access to your own Search Console and GA4 accounts. I read the reports you already hold. I do not contact your agency.

### Do you need logins to our website or the agency's tools?

No. My SEO agency review needs only read-only Google Search Console and GA4 access plus the reports and contract you already have. I audit the public site with a crawler.

### Is this a sales pitch for your retainer?

No. My SEO agency review is a fixed £495 piece of work with no obligation to buy anything else. I will say so and suggest you renew if the evidence shows your agency is doing well.

### Can you review a PPC or paid social agency?

No. My agency review covers SEO and AI-search work only. Ask a specialist in paid media for that channel.

### What if our site has more than 500 pages?

Sites over around 500 pages need a separate scope and price for the SEO agency review. The same applies to multiple international versions and a recent migration. I confirm this before any paid work starts.

### How far back do you look?

My SEO agency review usually covers the full contract period where it fits inside the 16 months of performance data that Google Search Console holds. Older reports are still useful for checking what was promised.

### Where are you based, and do you work with businesses outside Berkshire?

I am based in Reading, Berkshire. I run the SEO agency review online for businesses anywhere in the UK. Access, the written findings and the walkthrough call all happen remotely.

